message: "Please cite this unrefereed mathematical candidate and preserve its scope qualifications."
title: "Uniformly most split reliable graphs: a complete answer outside two edge counts"
type: article
authors:
  - name: Anonymous
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23450265
date-released: 2026-10-18
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipitchford/uniform-split-reliability"
license: CC0-1.0
abstract: >-
  An unrefereed candidate classifies existence of uniformly most split reliable
  graphs outside two edge counts at every order n>=7, completes the classification
  through n=51 using exact finite certificates, and proves sufficient cone
  comparisons on explicit all-order probability intervals. The unrestricted-order
  middle interval and the two uniform boundary cases remain unresolved.
